      "writtenOn": "2024-03-08T03:20:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Does this change the behavior?\nPreviously, it seems this method add `getProviderIfaceStats` to the entry if value is not UNSUPPORTED.\n\nI think having helper method allow us to use the same flow with `getUidStats`.\n```\nprivate NetworkStats.Entry getIfaceStatsInternal(@NonNull String iface, int type) {\n  final NetworkStats.Entry entry \u003d nativeGetIfaceStat(iface);\n  if(entry \u003d\u003d null) {\n        return null;\n  }\n  entry.add(getProviderIfaceStats(iface));\n  return entry;\n}\n\n@Override\npublic long getIfaceStats(@NonNull String iface, int type) {\n    Objects.requireNonNull(iface);\n    if (!isEntryValueTypeValid(type)) return UNSUPPORTED;\n\n    if (!mSupportTrafficStatsRateLimitCache) {\n       return getEntryValueForType(getIfaceStatsInternal(iface, type), type);\n    }\n\n    NetworkStats.Entry cachedEntry \u003d mTrafficStatsIfaceCache.get(iface, UID_ALL);\n    if (cachedEntry !\u003d null) {\n       return getEntryValueForType(cachedEntry, type);\n    }\n\n    final NetworkStats.Entry entry \u003d getIfaceStatsInternal((iface, type);\n    if (entry !\u003d null \u0026\u0026 !entry.isEmpty()) {\n        mTrafficStatsUidCache.put(iface, UID_ALL, entry);\n    }\n        \n    return getEntryValueForType(entry, type);\n}\n```\n\nSame for `getTotalStats`",
